New bug, found by the owner on screen: save a script in Final Draft while it's open in eDraft → eDraft reloads it via ScreenplayDocument.swift:94 → applyExternalSource → the page view shows a dark gap band cutting through a line of text. The pagination and the laid text disagree after an external reload. This is the third bug in one family (page-tear IL-0089, collapsed-cut IL-0095, now external-reload) — three symptoms, one root: page geometry can be computed from a different version of the text than what's on screen. I do NOT want a patch. I want the root gone: investigate whether one invariant can be made unrepresentable — gap bands, page starts and sheet boundaries always derive from the same laid elements in one place, for EVERY entry path (edit, undo, external reload, resize, omit). If that refactor is the real fix, size it honestly and propose it. First step either way: a failing test that drives an external-source change into a multi-page document and asserts every band sits at a real page boundary of the laid text. Vibe Check first, wait for my yes.